# Laziness proof: $map over dict preserves thunks in unused values
# The mapped dict contains an error in y's value (division by zero),
# but because we only access x, the error is never triggered.
# This proves that $map does NOT eagerly materialize dict values.
[map [fn [let v] [+ v 10]] [x: 1  y: [/ 1 0]]]
---
%.x
=== out
Int(11)
